{
  "_comment": [
    "Provider selection, one entry per leg. THIS .example SHIPS ALL LEGS ON 'none'",
    "so a fresh clone runs and reports INFERRED/ABSENT rather than fabricating a",
    "pass. Copy it to providers.json (gitignored) and point the legs at what you",
    "actually have.",
    "",
    "Run `python3 tools/fundamentals.py --list-providers` to see what is installed.",
    "",
    "fundamentals — 'derived' needs no subscription: it rebuilds a composite from",
    "free Yahoo data and marks every row approximate. Calibrated 18 Aug 2026,",
    "r=0.88 vs a curated scorer. See docs/DERIVED_CALIBRATION_2026-08-18.md.",
    "",
    "flow / conviction — there is no free substitute for either, and that is fine.",
    "DATA_SOURCES.md is explicit: drop a leg you cannot source rather than proxy",
    "it. 'none' renders them ABSENT and the rules already handle that.",
    "",
    "fallback fires ONLY when the primary returns FAIL for a ticker. Setting it to",
    "'none' is rejected: a primary failure must not silently fabricate data. Use",
    "null to disable it."
  ],
  "fundamentals": { "provider": "none", "fallback": null },
  "flow":         { "provider": "none", "fallback": null },
  "conviction":   { "provider": "none", "fallback": null }
}
